-This is bad.

507
00:20:26,086 --> 00:20:29,089
-And that ain't good.
-Ho, ho.

508
00:20:29,124 --> 00:20:31,402
Ow!
-And Satan scores.

509
00:20:31,437 --> 00:20:33,232
-Darn that Devil.

510
00:20:33,266 --> 00:20:34,647
Oh, I'm sorry,

511
00:20:34,681 --> 00:20:37,926
but that old Devil is always
annoying me with his mischief.

512
00:20:37,960 --> 00:20:39,203
-If I could only go
down there now,

513
00:20:39,238 --> 00:20:41,516
I'd put him in his place.
-Oh, big talker.

514
00:20:41,550 --> 00:20:43,449
-But everyone knows
I can only go down to Earth

515
00:20:43,483 --> 00:20:45,416
on Christmas Eve,
and not before.

516
00:20:45,451 --> 00:20:48,281
-In the meantime...
[Speaking foreign language]

517
00:20:48,316 --> 00:20:50,870
[Speaking foreign language]

518
00:20:50,904 --> 00:20:52,320
-Huh?
-A short while ago,

519
00:20:52,354 --> 00:20:54,805
I saw the Devil whispering
to four children,

520
00:20:54,839 --> 00:20:56,496
and one was a poor little girl.

521
00:20:56,531 --> 00:20:58,326
-Narc.
-Do you know who they are?

522
00:20:58,360 --> 00:21:00,293
-I've got their names.
The bad boys are --

523
00:21:00,328 --> 00:21:02,019
-No, no, no, no, no, no.
-Oh, no, no, no, no.

524
00:21:02,053 --> 00:21:03,745
-The naughty boys
are not important.

525
00:21:03,779 --> 00:21:05,678
They will get punished
in due course.

526
00:21:05,712 --> 00:21:07,921
The ones I must reward
are the other children,

527
00:21:07,956 --> 00:21:09,371
like the good little girl.

528
00:21:09,406 --> 00:21:10,786
-I've got their names
right here.

529
00:21:10,821 --> 00:21:12,961
The girl is called --
-Uh, better look through

530
00:21:12,995 --> 00:21:14,549
the telescope, Pedro.
-What?

531
00:21:14,583 --> 00:21:16,758
-We'll find out
what they're doing.

532
00:21:16,792 --> 00:21:18,173
-There's a sliver?
-This is Santa's

533
00:21:18,207 --> 00:21:19,830
magic observatory.

534
00:21:19,864 --> 00:21:22,729
What wonderful instruments.
The year scope.

535
00:21:22,764 --> 00:21:24,766
The tele talker
that knows everything.

536
00:21:24,800 --> 00:21:26,319
The cosmic telescope.

537
00:21:26,354 --> 00:21:28,252
The master eye.
-The pleasure mouth.

538
00:21:28,287 --> 00:21:30,944
-Nothing that happens on Earth
is unknown to Santa Claus.

539
00:21:30,979 --> 00:21:34,189
-Thanks to Liz Smith.
-By thy magic powers,

540
00:21:34,223 --> 00:21:36,329
look for the child
we're seeking,

541
00:21:36,364 --> 00:21:39,953
whether she is in a cave
or behind a million mountains.

542
00:21:39,988 --> 00:21:42,439
-Wow, Santa's got the dirt
on everybody.

543
00:21:46,132 --> 00:21:47,306
-That is a mouth, isn't it?

544
00:21:47,340 --> 00:21:51,344
-All ready.

545
00:21:51,379 --> 00:21:53,622
-Whoa.

546
00:21:53,657 --> 00:21:55,900
-Santa's tendrils reach
far and wide.

547
00:21:55,935 --> 00:21:59,041
There is no hiding
from the Claus organization.

548
00:21:59,076 --> 00:22:04,978
♪♪

549
00:22:05,013 --> 00:22:07,326
-Huh? What? Huh?
Oh, Sandy Duncan.

550
00:22:07,360 --> 00:22:08,603
Ha.

551
00:22:08,637 --> 00:22:10,743
-Kid's positioning himself
to replace Santa.

552
00:22:10,777 --> 00:22:16,438
♪♪

553
00:22:16,473 --> 00:22:17,853
-Uh, yeah.

554
00:22:17,888 --> 00:22:19,545
-This weird enough for you,
folks?

555
00:22:19,579 --> 00:22:23,134
How does this make you feel
about Santa?

556
00:22:23,169 --> 00:22:25,378
-I think I found the girl?
-Where?

557
00:22:25,413 --> 00:22:27,725
-A dame? Spread out, kid.

558
00:22:27,760 --> 00:22:31,280
-In Mexico.

559
00:22:31,315 --> 00:22:34,525
-[Laughs] Oh, yeah,
he really zeroed in on her.

560
00:22:34,560 --> 00:22:39,530
♪♪

561
00:22:39,565 --> 00:22:40,876
-Oh.

562
00:22:40,911 --> 00:22:43,051
-♪ Incense and peppermints

563
00:22:45,536 --> 00:22:48,332
-"Puppet Master 3."

564
00:22:48,367 --> 00:22:50,645
-Yes, it's Lupita, all right.
-Huh.

565
00:22:50,679 --> 00:22:53,026
-And she's still dreaming
about that doll she wants.

566
00:22:53,061 --> 00:22:54,373
-Oh, it looks like
the puppet version

567
00:22:54,407 --> 00:22:56,098
of "My Dinner With Andre."

568
00:22:56,133 --> 00:22:59,826
-Satan's been busy, I see.

569
00:22:59,861 --> 00:23:02,277
[Laughter]

570
00:23:02,311 --> 00:23:07,800
♪♪

571
00:23:07,834 --> 00:23:13,357
♪♪

572
00:23:13,392 --> 00:23:17,672
[Cheers and applause]

573
00:23:17,706 --> 00:23:19,121
-Good evening, Buffalo.

574
00:23:19,156 --> 00:23:23,471
We are Santa Klaws, and we have
just one question for you.

575
00:23:23,505 --> 00:23:26,474
Are you ready to be merry?
-Yes.

576
00:23:26,508 --> 00:23:29,097
-I said, are you ready
to be merry?

577
00:23:29,131 --> 00:23:30,650
-Yes!

578
00:23:30,685 --> 00:23:32,376
-Then stuff this
in your stocking.

579
00:23:32,411 --> 00:23:34,205
One, two, three, four.

580
00:23:34,240 --> 00:23:39,003
-♪ I have slain the Grinch
I have broken his spell ♪

581
00:23:40,867 --> 00:23:45,562
♪ I am the warrior of Christmas,the world we will tell ♪

582
00:23:47,253 --> 00:23:49,980
-♪ Christmas time,
free your mind ♪

583
00:23:50,014 --> 00:23:53,466
♪ Let love unwind

584
00:23:53,501 --> 00:24:00,162
-♪ The warrior of Christmas
has cast out the neon prince ♪

585
00:24:00,197 --> 00:24:06,652
♪ Hail the new Claus,
your hair he will rinse ♪

586
00:24:06,686 --> 00:24:08,377
[Cheers and applause]

587
00:24:12,658 --> 00:24:16,834
-♪ Silver bells fall
from your nose ♪

588
00:24:16,869 --> 00:24:20,113
♪ Santa Claus and mistletoe

589
00:24:20,148 --> 00:24:22,495
♪ Rudolph's found
the emperor's clothes ♪

590
00:24:22,530 --> 00:24:25,636
-♪ Blitzen, let's explore

591
00:24:25,671 --> 00:24:28,674
♪ Joy to the woooooooorld

592
00:24:28,708 --> 00:24:32,505
Oh!

593
00:24:32,540 --> 00:24:33,989
-Thank you.

594
00:24:34,024 --> 00:24:35,750
-Thank you, Buffalo.
We love you.

595
00:24:35,784 --> 00:24:37,752
-Thank you.
Thank you.

596
00:24:37,786 --> 00:24:39,512
We love you.
-Thank you.

597
00:24:39,547 --> 00:24:41,549
♪♪

598
00:24:42,929 --> 00:24:46,519
-[Speaking indistinctly]

599
00:24:46,554 --> 00:24:48,210
-Huh?
-Oh, no.

600
00:24:48,245 --> 00:24:50,178
This is wrong somehow.

601
00:24:50,212 --> 00:24:52,491
-[Sighs]

602
00:24:52,525 --> 00:24:57,392
-We can only hope that
the scars don't go too deep.

603
00:24:57,426 --> 00:24:59,394
Come on, I gotta go look
for a slip.

604
00:25:02,466 --> 00:25:05,780
-And now the hollow feeling
that follows any puppet show.

605
00:25:05,814 --> 00:25:08,714
-Huh?

606
00:25:08,748 --> 00:25:11,475
-Lupita isn't thinking of
stealing that doll, is she.

607
00:25:11,510 --> 00:25:13,650
-Society owes me.
-No! No, Lupita.

608
00:25:13,684 --> 00:25:15,479
You shouldn't steal.
Put it back.

609
00:25:15,514 --> 00:25:17,205
-Oh, I'm sorry.
I'm the narrator.

610
00:25:17,239 --> 00:25:19,448
I shouldn't get so involved.

611
00:25:19,483 --> 00:25:22,210
-Huh?
-Lupita.

612
00:25:22,244 --> 00:25:23,452
Lupita, come here.

613
00:25:23,487 --> 00:25:26,663
-Run, Lupita, run.

614
00:25:26,697 --> 00:25:29,631
-Do I need accessories too?

615
00:25:32,254 --> 00:25:35,948
I'm at a moral crossroads, Mom.

616
00:25:35,982 --> 00:25:38,813
Aw.
-It's yours.

617
00:25:38,847 --> 00:25:41,022
Nobody saw you take it, Lupita.

618
00:25:41,056 --> 00:25:42,575
They have more,
and they won't miss it.

619
00:25:42,610 --> 00:25:44,163
What does one little
doll matter?

620
00:25:44,197 --> 00:25:45,854
Don't you see?

621
00:25:45,889 --> 00:25:47,580
You haven't got any toys.

622
00:25:47,615 --> 00:25:52,102
-He makes a convincing argument.-Don't listen to him, Lupita.

623
00:25:52,136 --> 00:25:53,413
It's bad to steal.

624
00:25:53,448 --> 00:25:54,760
And you'll be sorry.

625
00:25:54,794 --> 00:25:57,279
-Ah, the classic battle
between evil and the narrator.

626
00:25:57,314 --> 00:25:59,765
-That's right, put it back.
-I guess that's better.

627
00:25:59,799 --> 00:26:02,975
-Good girl.
-[Muttering in frustration]

628
00:26:03,009 --> 00:26:06,426
-Oh. Don't you ever
do that again.

629
00:26:09,878 --> 00:26:13,054
-Way to defeat Satan, honey.

630
00:26:13,088 --> 00:26:15,988
-How are you gonna fence a doll?

631
00:26:18,956 --> 00:26:21,856
-Oh, geez.
-Hey, silly girl.

632
00:26:21,890 --> 00:26:24,444
Now you'll have to do
without a dolly.

633
00:26:24,479 --> 00:26:26,930
Little girls must deal or do
without the things they like.

634
00:26:26,964 --> 00:26:30,416
-That's not true, Lupita.

635
00:26:30,450 --> 00:26:33,074
If you're good,
somehow you'll be rewarded.

636
00:26:33,108 --> 00:26:35,248
-Well, that's not strictly
true either, but...

637
00:26:35,283 --> 00:26:38,148
-Help me.

638
00:26:42,462 --> 00:26:44,568
-Hmm.

639
00:26:44,603 --> 00:26:46,777
-Cable pays off in so many ways.

640
00:26:46,812 --> 00:26:48,952
Ha.
-Hooray for her.

641
00:26:48,986 --> 00:26:50,194
Hooray for her.

642
00:26:50,229 --> 00:26:52,645
All my friends
can ignore the Devil.

643
00:26:52,680 --> 00:26:55,475
All they need to win
is to be good in spirit.

644
00:26:55,510 --> 00:26:59,134
-And the other children?
-Come, Pedro, find them.

645
00:26:59,169 --> 00:27:02,172
-Round up the usual suspects.

646
00:27:02,206 --> 00:27:04,968
-Santa's top executive, Pedro.

647
00:27:05,002 --> 00:27:09,455
-By thy magic powers, look for
the child we're seeking,

648
00:27:09,489 --> 00:27:13,217
whether he is in a cave
or behind a million mountains.

649
00:27:13,252 --> 00:27:14,460
Okay.

650
00:27:14,494 --> 00:27:17,774
-Now, Pedro, did I tell you
to summon demons?

651
00:27:17,808 --> 00:27:18,913
-We got dolls.

652
00:27:18,947 --> 00:27:22,917
-It's the "Trilogy of Terror"
dolls.

653
00:27:22,951 --> 00:27:24,228
-So where's Mrs. Claus?

654
00:27:24,263 --> 00:27:26,506
-Oh, she winters in Lauderdale.
-Oh.

655
00:27:26,541 --> 00:27:28,405
[high-pitched tones]

656
00:27:28,439 --> 00:27:31,270
-Ow.

657
00:27:31,304 --> 00:27:33,859
-Do I have tinnitus,
or does anyone else hear that?

658
00:27:33,893 --> 00:27:35,619
-What?

659
00:27:35,654 --> 00:27:37,759
-Increasingly paranoid,
Santa's obsession

660
00:27:37,794 --> 00:27:40,935
with security begins
to hinder everyday operations.

661
00:27:43,765 --> 00:27:45,077
-Uh, shouldn't Santa have

662
00:27:45,111 --> 00:27:49,460
a bench warrant
to install these things?

663
00:27:49,495 --> 00:27:52,947
-Mm, sugar plums.
Dancing. Ah.

664
00:27:52,981 --> 00:27:55,018
-He's sleeping soundly.

665
00:27:55,052 --> 00:27:57,572
His dream will appear
on the dream scope.

666
00:27:57,606 --> 00:27:58,711
-Hey, that's wrong.

667
00:27:58,746 --> 00:28:01,645
-Connect the antenna
for the dream scope.

668
00:28:01,680 --> 00:28:04,337
-Magic kiss carpets.

669
00:28:04,372 --> 00:28:06,512
-Hey, a Van Gogh fan.

670
00:28:06,546 --> 00:28:08,169
-Ow.

671
00:28:10,309 --> 00:28:13,277
-Well, Pedro, what's on
the dessert tray, huh?

672
00:28:15,970 --> 00:28:18,006
-Pop-O-Matic pops the dice.

673
00:28:20,940 --> 00:28:23,184
-It's the ultimate bubble.

674
00:28:25,842 --> 00:28:29,155
[Coughing]

675
00:28:29,190 --> 00:28:31,399
-No, not that dream. No.

676
00:28:31,433 --> 00:28:33,677
-Let's watch the little
rich boy's dream.

677
00:28:33,712 --> 00:28:35,575
-And the corruption inherent
in his life.

678
00:28:35,610 --> 00:28:38,993
-How strange.
And what large gift boxes.

679
00:28:39,027 --> 00:28:41,754
Would these be toys?

680
00:28:41,789 --> 00:28:44,481
Why, they contain
what a child loves best...

681
00:28:44,515 --> 00:28:46,586
-A maitre d'.
-...his parents.

682
00:28:48,727 --> 00:28:52,558
-It's your new mom.
-Ah.

683
00:28:52,592 --> 00:28:54,491
-Hey, this is a dream --
a two-parent house.

684
00:28:54,525 --> 00:28:56,148
-I see.

685
00:28:58,322 --> 00:28:59,945
-We need to go
and leave you again.

686
00:28:59,979 --> 00:29:02,844
The baby sitter is in the box
over in the corner.

687
00:29:02,879 --> 00:29:05,847
-I miss my mom.

688
00:29:05,882 --> 00:29:10,403
-[Speaking foreign language]

689
00:29:10,438 --> 00:29:13,648
-A dream is a wish
that the heart makes.

690
00:29:13,682 --> 00:29:14,856
-Or something like that.

691
00:29:14,891 --> 00:29:16,271
-Then this child is not worthy.

692
00:29:16,306 --> 00:29:19,792
He gets everything he wishes
just by asking his parents.

693
00:29:19,827 --> 00:29:21,829
-The only thing this child
wants --

694
00:29:21,863 --> 00:29:23,796
-Is fear itself.
-...is the love of his parents.

695
00:29:23,831 --> 00:29:25,729
-Don't they love him?

696
00:29:25,764 --> 00:29:27,869
-Maybe they do.

697
00:29:27,904 --> 00:29:30,216
And maybe they don't.
-Oh, geez, he's waffling.

698
00:29:30,251 --> 00:29:31,700
-But soon we will
find out the truth.

699
00:29:31,735 --> 00:29:32,667
-And Lupita?

700
00:29:32,701 --> 00:29:34,289
What do you think
she might wish?

701
00:29:34,324 --> 00:29:38,293
-If she's already sleeping, we
might be able to see her dream.

702
00:29:38,328 --> 00:29:40,813
-Kids, this is so Jungian.

703
00:29:44,541 --> 00:29:46,405
-Santa. Uh, Santa, yo.

704
00:29:46,439 --> 00:29:50,409
-Hey, Kringle, snap out of it!
Geez! Whoa.

705
00:29:50,443 --> 00:29:53,792
[Coughing]

706
00:29:53,826 --> 00:29:55,621
-Huh?

707
00:29:55,655 --> 00:29:58,693
Honey, Santa's looking in
on our daughter again.

708
00:29:58,727 --> 00:30:01,144
-Honey, does this crowbar
look okay here?

709
00:30:04,595 --> 00:30:05,873
-Well, they're not too poor
to afford

710
00:30:05,907 --> 00:30:07,875
an insurance calendar, I see.

711
00:30:11,499 --> 00:30:14,813
-It was nice of Marcel Duchamp
to let them use his apartment.

712
00:30:14,847 --> 00:30:18,955
♪♪

713
00:30:18,989 --> 00:30:20,991
-I wonder if our child
is dreaming.

714
00:30:21,026 --> 00:30:22,993
-Well, actually we enter
several dream stages

715
00:30:23,028 --> 00:30:24,857
during a typical night.
There's REM.

716
00:30:24,892 --> 00:30:26,479
Then there's the --
Oh, sorry.

717
00:30:26,514 --> 00:30:27,826
-Let's go bowling.

718
00:30:27,860 --> 00:30:29,655
-I recall when
I was a little girl.

719
00:30:29,689 --> 00:30:30,725
-Oh, God, here we go.

720
00:30:30,759 --> 00:30:32,313
-I often would dream
of great riches.

721
00:30:32,347 --> 00:30:33,797
-The old "I could have been
a dancer" story.

722
00:30:33,832 --> 00:30:35,281
-But I have all the things
I wish for

723
00:30:35,316 --> 00:30:38,112
and not a care in the world.

724
00:30:38,146 --> 00:30:41,149
-That was before the abysmal
mess called my marriage.

725
00:30:41,184 --> 00:30:43,703
Sorry. Sorry.
-Confounded Devil.

726
00:30:43,738 --> 00:30:45,740
Why can't he leave Lupita alone?

727
00:30:45,774 --> 00:30:48,916
-Hey, he's just doing his job.

728
00:30:48,950 --> 00:30:51,608
-Whoa, his breath smells
like Underwood Deviled Ham.

729
00:30:51,642 --> 00:30:53,817
-[Snoring]

730
00:30:53,852 --> 00:30:55,923
-[Panting]

731
00:30:55,957 --> 00:30:59,098
-I think he got those horns
in Jackson Hole, Wyoming.

732
00:30:59,133 --> 00:31:02,101
-Maybe his breath
is fresh and minty.

733
00:31:02,136 --> 00:31:03,378
-Ooh.
-That's disgusting.

734
00:31:03,413 --> 00:31:06,381
-Just look at that old busybody.

735
00:31:06,416 --> 00:31:09,281
He'll make Lupita
want to steal again.

736
00:31:09,315 --> 00:31:11,490
He'll be part of her dream.

737
00:31:11,524 --> 00:31:13,319
-[Imitating child] Uh, Santa,
could you notch the volume

738
00:31:13,354 --> 00:31:14,769
down a little?
We're right here.

739
00:31:14,803 --> 00:31:16,736
-Better look at her dream now.

740
00:31:16,771 --> 00:31:19,947
-Better get on the horn with Godsince Satan's involved now.

741
00:31:23,226 --> 00:31:25,780
-Pick your refrigerator, Lupita.

742
00:31:25,814 --> 00:31:29,646
-♪ I can get a dolly,
and the top is blue ♪

743
00:31:29,680 --> 00:31:33,305
♪ She is very pretty,
and her name is Sue ♪

744
00:31:33,339 --> 00:31:34,720
-Everybody sing along.

745
00:31:34,754 --> 00:31:36,618
- ♪ When I took her shopping,
she got sick... ♪

746
00:31:36,653 --> 00:31:38,517
-Must admit,
she's got a way with a ballad.

747
00:31:38,551 --> 00:31:40,657
-♪ When I took her home,
she got well... ♪

748
00:31:40,691 --> 00:31:42,210
-Take it home, Lupita.

749
00:31:42,245 --> 00:31:48,044
♪♪

750
00:31:49,424 --> 00:31:51,599
-Why don't you steal us?
We can all be yours.

751
00:31:51,633 --> 00:31:52,496
-No.

752
00:31:52,531 --> 00:31:54,636
You know that stealing is bad.

753
00:31:54,671 --> 00:31:57,432
And I want to be good.
-But you must learn to steal.

754
00:31:57,467 --> 00:32:00,366
-I'm Martha Raye.
-No. You know stealing is bad.

755
00:32:00,401 --> 00:32:02,023
And I want to be good.

756
00:32:02,058 --> 00:32:04,508
-We dolls don't like
good little girls.

757
00:32:04,543 --> 00:32:05,820
-No.

