00:42:38,763 --> 00:42:40,454
-He's really going
downhill fast.

1001
00:42:40,488 --> 00:42:43,388
-Well, just to make sure,
why don't you take it with you?

1002
00:42:43,422 --> 00:42:45,010
-I've really got to hurry.

1003
00:42:45,045 --> 00:42:47,116
It's almost time
for the crystal clock

1004
00:42:47,150 --> 00:42:48,773
on the wall to strike 10:00.

1005
00:42:48,807 --> 00:42:51,223
-Don't forget that you've got
to return

1006
00:42:51,258 --> 00:42:53,571
to the castle ahead
of the sunrise,

1007
00:42:53,605 --> 00:42:57,471
because the sun will turn
the reindeer into dust.

1008
00:42:57,505 --> 00:42:59,162
-How many Christmases
you done, kid?

1009
00:42:59,197 --> 00:43:00,612
-I'll be here, all right.

1010
00:43:00,647 --> 00:43:02,959
In that case, I couldn't
get back to the castle.

1011
00:43:02,994 --> 00:43:05,272
And on what they use for food,
I'd perish.

1012
00:43:05,306 --> 00:43:08,275
Because here our main food
is pastries and ice cream

1013
00:43:08,309 --> 00:43:09,621
made of soft clouds --

1014
00:43:09,656 --> 00:43:11,347
[Gagging]

1015
00:43:11,381 --> 00:43:13,729
-What food do they eat
on Earth, Santa Claus?

1016
00:43:13,763 --> 00:43:15,040
-Oh, everything in sight.

1017
00:43:15,075 --> 00:43:18,250
They eat most of the animals,
the plants, the flowers,

1018
00:43:18,285 --> 00:43:21,633
the roots, birds,
even smoke and alcohol.

1019
00:43:21,668 --> 00:43:23,704
-And they eat at Hardee's.
-But enough of this talking.

1020
00:43:23,739 --> 00:43:25,741
We're wasting time,
and I must be off.

1021
00:43:25,775 --> 00:43:27,535
[Beeping]

1022
00:43:27,570 --> 00:43:29,952
-Nice van horn, Kringle.

1023
00:43:29,986 --> 00:43:35,060
-♪ I'm not scared of dying,
and I don't really care ♪

1024
00:43:35,095 --> 00:43:36,337
-Everybody.

1025
00:43:36,372 --> 00:43:39,547
-♪ Merry Christmas,
everybody, everybody ♪

1026
00:43:39,582 --> 00:43:41,895
♪ Say goodbye to Santa Claus

1027
00:43:41,929 --> 00:43:43,413
♪ He is leaving...

1028
00:43:43,448 --> 00:43:45,070
-Hope they know
they're not going with.

1029
00:43:45,105 --> 00:43:46,451
♪ ...with the reindeer

1030
00:43:46,485 --> 00:43:49,350
♪ And a sack of Christmas toys

1031
00:43:49,385 --> 00:43:52,077
-[Imitating smashing sounds]

1032
00:43:56,495 --> 00:43:59,602
-Well, only 37 billion
gifts to go.

1033
00:43:59,637 --> 00:44:01,880
-♪ Hurry up, my children

1034
00:44:01,915 --> 00:44:04,020
♪ Get on with your packing

1035
00:44:04,055 --> 00:44:08,197
♪ It's the night for Santa Clausto fill all those stockings ♪

1036
00:44:08,231 --> 00:44:09,750
-Nice aria, Santa.

1037
00:44:09,785 --> 00:44:11,925
-[Children singing]

1038
00:44:11,959 --> 00:44:14,168
-Thanks a lot, Rolf.

1039
00:44:18,759 --> 00:44:23,212
-♪ Merry, merry greetings
I take to one and all ♪

1040
00:44:23,246 --> 00:44:26,767
♪ So hurry if you want to enjoy
the Yuletide fun ♪

1041
00:44:26,802 --> 00:44:29,149
-♪ I'll see you in your
nightmares ♪

1042
00:44:29,183 --> 00:44:30,875
♪ Rum-pum, pum-pum-pum

1043
00:44:30,909 --> 00:44:32,117
[Smashing sounds]

1044
00:44:32,152 --> 00:44:37,398
-Hey, my Ovation.
-This will be mine one day.

1045
00:44:37,433 --> 00:44:39,055
-Bone in my hair?
I'm from Detroit.

1046
00:44:39,090 --> 00:44:41,126
-Now Merry Christmas.

1047
00:44:41,161 --> 00:44:42,887
Merry Christmas to all.

1048
00:44:42,921 --> 00:44:44,267
-Merry Christmas.

1049
00:44:44,302 --> 00:44:47,063
-Every year we've got to sing
a fruity send-off song.

1050
00:44:47,098 --> 00:44:48,755
No wonder the elves quit.

1051
00:44:48,789 --> 00:44:51,309
-[Chuckles]

1052
00:44:51,343 --> 00:44:54,070
-Let's see if I have everything.

1053
00:44:54,105 --> 00:44:58,143
The bag with the powders for
dreaming of joy and goodwill.

1054
00:44:58,178 --> 00:45:01,215
-Hey, it's Closey,
the closed caption kid.

1055
00:45:01,250 --> 00:45:02,907
-The golden key that opens
all doors.

1056
00:45:02,941 --> 00:45:05,703
-Cuckoo, cuckoo, cuckoo.
-The sleigh.

1057
00:45:05,737 --> 00:45:08,809
And now I'd better make sure
my reindeer are running.

1058
00:45:08,844 --> 00:45:10,984
-So I'm OD'd
on whimsy right now.

1059
00:45:11,018 --> 00:45:14,642
-Yes, Santa's sleigh is really
a huge toy sleigh.

1060
00:45:14,677 --> 00:45:16,023
-No!
-And he has to wind it

1061
00:45:16,058 --> 00:45:19,199
like any other toy
to make it go.

1062
00:45:19,233 --> 00:45:22,167
-Oh, kind of technical here.
You wouldn't understand.

1063
00:45:22,202 --> 00:45:24,480
-It lives.

1064
00:45:24,514 --> 00:45:29,554
-Oh, Santa, you miracle worker.

1065
00:45:29,588 --> 00:45:30,797
-Ha. Hey, Mike.
-Yeah?

1066
00:45:30,831 --> 00:45:33,523
-That deer is feeling
pretty cranky right now.

1067
00:45:33,558 --> 00:45:35,456
Ha! Get it?
Cranky. Ha.

1068
00:45:35,491 --> 00:45:37,527
Deer. Ha. It --

1069
00:45:37,562 --> 00:45:40,323
[Groans]

1070
00:45:43,016 --> 00:45:44,672
-No.
This isn't charming at all.

1071
00:45:44,707 --> 00:45:46,571
It's creepy.

1072
00:45:50,299 --> 00:45:53,923
-Help us.
-[Laughing]

1073
00:45:53,958 --> 00:45:57,824
-Well, when Santa laughs,the whole world shakes its head.

1074
00:45:57,858 --> 00:46:02,069
[Laughter]

1075
00:46:02,104 --> 00:46:06,729
[Hysterical forced laughter]

1076
00:46:06,764 --> 00:46:09,939
-My God, what's happening?

1077
00:46:09,974 --> 00:46:12,942
-Huh.
-Santa?

1078
00:46:12,977 --> 00:46:16,221
-Uh, a pentagram and reindeer
laughing.

1079
00:46:16,256 --> 00:46:17,671
You figure it out.

1080
00:46:17,705 --> 00:46:20,294
[ "Jingle Bells"playing]

1081
00:46:20,329 --> 00:46:22,020
-Be off, my reindeer,

1082
00:46:22,055 --> 00:46:25,748
and glide through the heavens
as fast as you can go.

1083
00:46:25,783 --> 00:46:29,579
May my palace of gold
and crystal enjoy peace.

1084
00:46:29,614 --> 00:46:32,790
And Jesus, the Son of God,
join us on Earth

1085
00:46:32,824 --> 00:46:35,758
so that we can
all have joy and goodwill.

1086
00:46:35,793 --> 00:46:38,416
-This is weird theology.
-On, my good reindeer!

1087
00:46:41,143 --> 00:46:43,524
-Wait, open the garage door!
Oh, that's --

1088
00:46:43,559 --> 00:46:46,355
[Imitates crashing noise]

1089
00:46:46,389 --> 00:46:48,288
-Well, Santa, I guess all us
3-year-olds

1090
00:46:48,322 --> 00:46:49,530
will just fend for ourselves.

1091
00:46:49,565 --> 00:46:52,119
Don't worry about us.

1092
00:46:52,154 --> 00:46:54,087
-So Mike, is this St. Cloud?

1093
00:46:54,121 --> 00:46:55,847
[Chuckling]
-That's two.

1094
00:46:55,882 --> 00:46:58,263
-Because it's clouds.

1095
00:47:01,888 --> 00:47:05,857
-Oh, darn, forgot my Chapstick.

1096
00:47:05,892 --> 00:47:07,686
Whatever.

1097
00:47:07,721 --> 00:47:08,826
-I'm telling you, Blixen,

1098
00:47:08,860 --> 00:47:10,897
he's gained about 30 pounds
since last year.

1099
00:47:10,931 --> 00:47:12,484
I don't think I can hold out.

1100
00:47:12,519 --> 00:47:15,142
[Panting]

1101
00:47:15,177 --> 00:47:17,524
-Uh, this is Houston, Santa.

1102
00:47:17,558 --> 00:47:18,697
We're tracking you on radar.

1103
00:47:18,732 --> 00:47:20,078
Seem to be having
some trouble there

1104
00:47:20,113 --> 00:47:21,424
with the primary thrust system.

1105
00:47:21,459 --> 00:47:24,600
Uh, repeat, eject now.
-Uh-oh.

1106
00:47:24,634 --> 00:47:28,949
Santa got drunk and deliveredall the gifts to the moon again.

1107
00:47:28,984 --> 00:47:30,951
-Whew, that was close.
-Well, no.

1108
00:47:30,986 --> 00:47:33,057
-He almost ran into the moon.

1109
00:47:33,091 --> 00:47:36,474
-Just take my word for it.

1110
00:47:36,508 --> 00:47:38,752
-And here's the planet Earth.

1111
00:47:38,786 --> 00:47:39,822
-Well, kind of.

1112
00:47:39,857 --> 00:47:42,204
-I wonder where Santa
will go first.

1113
00:47:42,238 --> 00:47:45,207
Europe? Africa? America?

1114
00:47:45,241 --> 00:47:48,175
- Circle Pines?

1115
00:47:48,210 --> 00:47:51,144
-♪ I like to live in America

1116
00:47:51,178 --> 00:47:53,456
♪ Cadillacs zoom in America

1117
00:47:57,219 --> 00:47:59,911
-Think of all the nice things
you'll get from Santa Claus.

1118
00:47:59,946 --> 00:48:01,637
-Yes, Mama.

1119
00:48:01,671 --> 00:48:02,810
-That's a good boy.
-Or a girl.

1120
00:48:02,845 --> 00:48:05,089
-See you in the morning.
-If you get bored,

1121
00:48:05,123 --> 00:48:07,505
you can go down
and practice your piano lesson.

1122
00:48:07,539 --> 00:48:09,369
See you later, my darling.

1123
00:48:09,403 --> 00:48:10,888
-Our love's implied.
Goodbye.

1124
00:48:10,922 --> 00:48:12,441
Maybe we can do this again
sometime.

1125
00:48:12,475 --> 00:48:15,754
You seem like a nice kid.
-Ugh.

1126
00:48:15,789 --> 00:48:18,896
Why do they leave me
so heavily medicated?

1127
00:48:18,930 --> 00:48:23,038
Um, were --
were my parents just here?

1128
00:48:23,072 --> 00:48:25,799
If I could just get
some movement in my legs.

1129
00:48:25,833 --> 00:48:28,733
[Whimpering]

1130
00:48:30,355 --> 00:48:32,530
-He's dead.
-I knew it.

1131
00:48:32,564 --> 00:48:33,738
The Devil is nearby,

1132
00:48:33,772 --> 00:48:36,465
and these three certainly
are up to no good.

1133
00:48:36,499 --> 00:48:37,984
-Okay, listen now.

1134
00:48:38,018 --> 00:48:40,607
As soon as Santa Claus lands
on the roof here,

1135
00:48:40,641 --> 00:48:42,402
all three of us
will jump on him.

1136
00:48:42,436 --> 00:48:44,645
-We'll tie him up
and we'll stick him in a sack.

1137
00:48:44,680 --> 00:48:47,579
And then we'll go home
with all of Santa's toys.

1138
00:48:47,614 --> 00:48:50,479
-But what about Santa?
-We can make him our slave,

1139
00:48:50,513 --> 00:48:52,757
and all of the candies
and toys will belong to us.

1140
00:48:52,791 --> 00:48:53,965
-Gee, nice kids.
-So whenever we want

1141
00:48:54,000 --> 00:48:56,416
something --
-Oh boy, this is gonna be fun.

1142
00:48:56,450 --> 00:48:58,004
-Better not talk now.

1143
00:48:58,038 --> 00:49:00,385
He can hear, so get away.

1144
00:49:00,420 --> 00:49:02,594
-Isn't kidnapping Santa
a federal offense?

1145
00:49:02,629 --> 00:49:05,701
-I think so.

1146
00:49:05,735 --> 00:49:10,223
-No, a strolling Gallagher.
-Ugh.

1147
00:49:10,257 --> 00:49:12,087
[Upbeat music playing]

1148
00:49:12,121 --> 00:49:15,331
-It's a Fellini Christmas.

1149
00:49:15,366 --> 00:49:18,438
-Attica! Attica!
-Time for bed.

1150
00:49:18,472 --> 00:49:21,544
Santa Claus will be here
any minute now.

1151
00:49:21,579 --> 00:49:25,755
-Mama, and who is Santa Claus?
-He's the man in the store,

1152
00:49:25,790 --> 00:49:27,516
the one with the red suit
and the white beard

1153
00:49:27,550 --> 00:49:29,311
that was laughing very much.

1154
00:49:29,345 --> 00:49:32,555
-And does Santa know about me?
-Uh-huh.

1155
00:49:32,590 --> 00:49:36,456
-Is he real, like my daddy?
-[Chuckles] No, not really.

1156
00:49:36,490 --> 00:49:39,459
-Would you shut
the bloody organ grinder up?

1157
00:49:39,493 --> 00:49:41,116
-Probably French.

1158
00:49:41,150 --> 00:49:44,188
-Hey.
-And comes here once a year.

1159
00:49:44,222 --> 00:49:45,879
-What does he come for?

1160
00:49:45,913 --> 00:49:48,744
-They say he gives those
to children who are obedient.

1161
00:49:48,778 --> 00:49:50,366
-I don't think he likes me.

1162
00:49:50,401 --> 00:49:54,163
He has never
brought me any dollies.

1163
00:49:54,198 --> 00:49:55,578
-It's --
-He's just jealous.

1164
00:49:55,613 --> 00:49:57,511
-...not that.

1165
00:49:57,546 --> 00:49:59,789
Maybe you're forgetting
to ask him for dollies.

1166
00:49:59,824 --> 00:50:04,311
-Yeah, bull!
-And if I ask him for one now?

1167
00:50:04,346 --> 00:50:06,831
-Go ahead.
-Make my day.

1168
00:50:06,865 --> 00:50:08,867
-Perhaps he'll hear you.

1169
00:50:08,902 --> 00:50:10,800
We can say a prayer, dear.

1170
00:50:10,835 --> 00:50:12,630
-Mama, please don't cry.

1171
00:50:12,664 --> 00:50:16,427
-You will stain my dress.
-It's just that it's Christmas.

1172
00:50:16,461 --> 00:50:19,671
And Christmas always
makes me feel sad.

1173
00:50:19,706 --> 00:50:21,915
-You and a lot of other people.

1174
00:50:21,949 --> 00:50:25,574
-Mommy, what is
Christmas good for.

1175
00:50:25,608 --> 00:50:29,612
-Well, to remind us that Christ
was born many years ago.

1176
00:50:29,647 --> 00:50:31,890
-Craig?
I don't think so.

1177
00:50:31,925 --> 00:50:34,065
-And he was even poorer
than we are.

1178
00:50:34,100 --> 00:50:35,308
-Whoa.

1179
00:50:35,342 --> 00:50:37,413
-He was born in a bed of straw.
-Know what, Mama?

1180
00:50:37,448 --> 00:50:38,759
-I don't buy it.

1181
00:50:38,794 --> 00:50:41,693
-I already asked Santa Claus
for two pretty dollies.

1182
00:50:41,728 --> 00:50:45,352
If he brings me two,
I'll give one to little Jesus.

1183
00:50:45,387 --> 00:50:47,630
-Oh, he's got plenty
of presents already.

1184
00:50:47,665 --> 00:50:50,047
-Yes, my darling.

1185
00:50:50,081 --> 00:50:53,567
Maybe if we pray
with all of our might, hmm?

1186
00:50:53,602 --> 00:50:55,259
-Oh, look at that.
The roof's leaking.

1187
00:50:55,293 --> 00:50:57,123
I thought I spackled that.

1188
00:50:57,157 --> 00:50:59,608
[ "Jingle Bells"playing]

1189
00:50:59,642 --> 00:51:02,300
-♪ Shotgun shells,
BB's in the air ♪

1190
00:51:02,335 --> 00:51:03,922
-If I don't find a break
in this cloud cover,

1191
00:51:03,957 --> 00:51:05,407
I'm never gonna make it.

1192
00:51:05,441 --> 00:51:07,409
-♪ Plink, plink, plink, plink

1193
00:51:07,443 --> 00:51:09,859
♪ Pizzicato plink, plink

1194
00:51:09,894 --> 00:51:11,206
♪ Come legato in

1195
00:51:11,240 --> 00:51:12,966
-♪ Knick-knack, paddywhack,
give a dog a bone ♪

1196
00:51:13,000 --> 00:51:15,417
-While Santa steers
his sleigh towards Earth --

1197
00:51:15,451 --> 00:51:16,694
-Disaster awaits.

1198
00:51:16,728 --> 00:51:20,318
-...old devil Pitch
awaits his arrival.

1199
00:51:20,353 --> 00:51:22,113
Here comes Santa now.

1200
00:51:22,148 --> 00:51:24,357
First stop, Mexico City.

1201
00:51:24,391 --> 00:51:26,807
-Manure dust
overtakes the sleigh.

1202
00:51:30,052 --> 00:51:32,089
-Oh, Santa,
I need some stuff, man.

1203
00:51:32,123 --> 00:51:34,021
Just a taste.
Come on, man.

1204
00:51:34,056 --> 00:51:36,162
-It's freezing.

1205
00:51:36,196 --> 00:51:39,544
I wish I were back in Hades,
tending the furnaces.

1206
00:51:39,579 --> 00:51:41,512
-[Santa Laughing]

1207
00:51:41,546 --> 00:51:42,858
-He's heard Santa.

1208
00:51:42,892 --> 00:51:46,310
-Well, I hope so,
with ears like that.

1209
00:51:46,344 --> 00:51:50,037
-Boy, he's really hauling ass.
-And it's his.

1210
00:51:50,072 --> 00:51:51,763
-By Satan, there he is.

1211
00:51:51,798 --> 00:51:53,351
I'm committed and I'm prepared
to upset

1212
00:51:53,386 --> 00:51:55,629
his own merry Christmas.
Heh, heh.

1213
00:51:55,664 --> 00:51:58,253
-I love my work.
-We will see who wins out.

1214
00:51:58,287 --> 00:52:01,152
This is one night
that no one can take from me.

1215
00:52:01,187 --> 00:52:05,398
-He has kind of
an oily complexion.

1216
00:52:05,432 --> 00:52:06,709
-What 's he going to do?

1217
00:52:06,744 --> 00:52:09,022
-You tell us.
-Oh-ho.

1218
00:52:09,056 --> 00:52:12,750
He's going to push the chimney
out of place so that poor old

1219
00:52:12,784 --> 00:52:14,786
Santa won't be able
to enter this house.

1220
00:52:14,821 --> 00:52:18,997
-Well, that nut.
[Chuckling]

1221
00:52:19,032 --> 00:52:21,414
-I love Ron Reagan Jr.

1222
00:52:21,448 --> 00:52:23,554
-Hmm.

1223
00:52:23,588 --> 00:52:25,418
Satan, honey, no.

1224
00:52:25,452 --> 00:52:29,629
Ooh.
-Don't ever do that again.

1225
00:52:29,663 --> 00:52:32,114
[Imitates vomiting]

1226
00:52:32,149 --> 00:52:35,117
-♪ The Devil is a wiener

1227
00:52:35,152 --> 00:52:37,982
♪ Wiener, wiener, wiener

1228
00:52:38,016 --> 00:52:41,572
-Well, I'll park
in the ramp this time.

1229
00:52:41,606 --> 00:52:43,263
-Don't do that with your hands.
Don't.

1230
00:52:43,298 --> 00:52:45,507
[ "Jingle Bells"playing]

1231
00:52:45,541 --> 00:52:53,411
♪♪

1232
00:52:53,446 --> 00:52:56,932
-[Imitating helicopter blades
whirring]

1233
00:52:56,966 --> 00:52:58,485
-So this is all the toys
in the world

1234
00:52:58,520 --> 00:53:00,142
for all the children
in the world?

1235
00:53:00,177 --> 00:53:01,971
-Yep.

1236
00:53:02,006 --> 00:53:04,595
-Hefty, hefty, hefty.

1237
00:53:04,629 --> 00:53:07,218
-Wimpy, wimpy, wimpy.

1238
00:53:09,151 --> 00:53:10,635
-[Groaning]

1239
00:53:12,982 --> 00:53:15,571
This is a very difficult move
for this actor.

1240
00:53:18,850 --> 00:53:20,749
-You know what, Santa?
It's about 4:00 a.m.

1241
00:53:20,783 --> 00:53:23,338
You'd better get a rush on.

1242
00:53:23,372 --> 00:53:26,306
-[Groaning]

1243
00:53:26,341 --> 00:53:29,102
-Terpsichore.

1244
00:53:29,136 --> 00:53:32,243
-Whew, that was
some action sequence.

1245
00:53:32,278 --> 00:53:33,417
Whew.
-I'm sweating.

1246
00:53:33,451 --> 00:53:35,626
-He's got a Stephen King
manuscript in that bag.

1247
00:53:35,660 --> 00:53:38,249
-Let's hope Santa realizes
what's happened.

1248
00:53:40,562 --> 00:53:41,873
-[Grunting]

1249
00:53:41,908 --> 00:53:43,150
-Huh?.

1250
00:53:43,185 --> 00:53:47,638
-Well, what's happened here?
I can smell sulfur.

1251
00:53:47,672 --> 00:53:50,261
-Oh, sorry, that was me.
-Well, that must explain this.

1252
00:53:50,296 --> 00:53:52,884
That old devil
Pitch must be around here.

1253
00:53:52,919 --> 00:53:55,404
[Grunting]

1254
00:53:55,439 --> 00:53:59,339
-Jim J. Bullock is more
frightening than that devil.

1255
00:53:59,374 --> 00:54:01,099
-[As Jim J. Bullock]
Hi, Mr. Rush.

1256
00:54:03,101 --> 00:54:05,518
-Santa's determined to get in.

1257
00:54:05,552 --> 00:54:07,105
He'll find a way.

1258
00:54:07,140 --> 00:54:08,866
He's not one to give up.

1259
00:54:11,282 --> 00:54:13,664
-O-ho, got some plastique
in here.

1260
00:54:13,698 --> 00:54:17,046
Fragmentation bomb.

1261
00:54:17,081 --> 00:54:20,395
-Well, time for a Mai Tai.

1262
00:54:20,429 --> 00:54:22,155
Big one, too.

1263
00:54:22,189 --> 00:54:24,571
-Well, there's more than one wayto beat the Devil.

1264
00:54:24,606 --> 00:54:27,402
Santa will jump down
using his magic parasol.

1265
00:54:27,436 --> 00:54:30,197
-With a 10-point
degree of difficulty.

1266
00:54:30,232 --> 00:54:31,889
-Old Pitch hadn't
counted on this.

1267
00:54:31,923 --> 00:54:34,650
-Doh! Doh! Doh!
-He's almost green with anger.

1268
00:54:37,515 --> 00:54:43,728
-And it took a fly gang of 16
to lower Santa down.

1269
00:54:43,763 --> 00:54:47,249
-Tuck and roll, Kringle,
tuck and roll.

1270
00:54:47,284 --> 00:54:48,906
-I'm frustrated.

1271
00:54:51,288 --> 00:54:53,773
-That's good.

1272
00:54:53,807 --> 00:54:55,602
-[Imitating alarm sounds]

1273
00:54:55,637 --> 00:54:58,329
-[Imitating dog barking]

1274
00:54:58,364 --> 00:55:01,505
[Doorknob rattling]

1275
00:55:01,539 --> 00:55:04,197
-It is the witching hour,
my friend.

1276
00:55:04,231 --> 00:55:06,061
-Uh-oh.

1277
00:55:06,095 --> 00:55:09,271
These two seem to knowthat Santa's in the living room.

1278
00:55:11,308 --> 00:55:13,068
Look out, Santa,
they'll see you.

1279
00:55:13,102 --> 00:55:15,933
-[Imitates shotgun racking
and firing]

1280
00:55:15,967 --> 00:55:17,314
-Yeah.

1281
00:55:17,348 --> 00:55:19,799
Well, that's the last thing
they'll ever see.

1282
00:55:19,833 --> 00:55:23,043
-Why, of course.
Santa can handle this.

1283
00:55:23,078 --> 00:55:25,218
All he has to do is use
the magic

1284
00:55:25,252 --> 00:55:27,531
dreaming powders prepared
by Mr. Merlin.

1285
00:55:27,565 --> 00:55:30,361
-And Mr. Owsley.

1286
00:55:30,396 --> 00:55:33,951
-And it isn't long before
our two little stay-up-lates

1287
00:55:33,985 --> 00:55:36,091
are sleeping soundly
in their bed.

1288
00:55:36,125 --> 00:55:38,887
-Unfortunately, the powder does
have contraindications

1289
00:55:38,921 --> 00:55:40,578
and enduring side effects.

1290
00:55:40,613 --> 00:55:43,926
-♪ It's the Devil's theme

1291
00:55:43,961 --> 00:55:46,101
♪ He's due for a little song

1292
00:55:46,135 --> 00:55:48,379
♪ Even though he's
the embodiment of evil ♪

1293
00:55:48,414 --> 00:55:50,761
♪ He's still got a goofy song

1294
00:55:50,795 --> 00:55:52,556
♪ In his tights
he brings death ♪

1295
00:55:52,590 --> 00:55:54,799
♪ Despair, disruption,
and disease ♪

1296
00:55:54,834 --> 00:55:59,114
♪ Now let's all join him,
and I'll laugh along ♪

1297
00:55:59,148 --> 00:56:01,496
Devil.
-Now what?

1298
00:56:01,530 --> 00:56:04,602
Must be Pitch putting
the chimney back in place.

1299
00:56:04,637 --> 00:56:05,948
-Son of a --

1300
00:56:05,983 --> 00:56:08,261
This time, I'm putting
my patent leather shoe down --

1301
00:56:08,295 --> 00:56:10,367
permanently.

1302
00:56:10,401 --> 00:56:13,956
-Ha. This year,
I gave everyone Yahtzee.

1303
00:56:13,991 --> 00:56:19,548
♪♪

1304
00:56:19,583 --> 00:56:21,550
[Imitates vomiting]

1305
00:56:25,658 --> 00:56:29,420
-Ha, ha.

1306
00:56:29,455 --> 00:56:32,319
-Hey, pitch black.
[Laughs]

1307
00:56:32,354 --> 00:56:36,047
Because of the --
-It's a living.

1308
00:56:36,082 --> 00:56:38,774
-[Chuckling]

1309
00:56:38,809 --> 00:56:41,467
-[Maniacal laughter]

1310
00:56:41,501 --> 00:56:51,477
♪♪

1311
00:56:51,511 --> 00:56:54,549
-Well, the Devil doesn't
give up either.

1312
00:56:54,583 --> 00:56:56,067
And he seems to be quite happy

1313
00:56:56,102 --> 00:56:59,208
about his next plot
against Santa.

1314
00:56:59,243 --> 00:57:00,762
-[Chuckling] No. No.

1315
00:57:00,796 --> 00:57:02,626
He enjoys pantaloons
more than he should.

1316
00:57:02,660 --> 00:57:04,455
[Rattling]

1317
00:57:04,490 --> 00:57:06,802
-Hey!

1318
00:57:06,837 --> 00:57:09,011
-Santa is filmed on location

1319
00:57:09,046 --> 00:57:11,566
with the men and women
of Broward County, Florida.

1320
00:57:14,707 --> 00:57:16,329
-Okay. Okay, if I join
your ranks,

1321
00:57:16,363 --> 00:57:18,607
will you stop dancing like that?

1322
00:57:18,642 --> 00:57:23,785
♪♪

1323
00:57:23,819 --> 00:57:26,166
-Could Santa be coming
down this chimney now?

1324
00:57:26,201 --> 00:57:27,133
-Yes.

1325
00:57:27,167 --> 00:57:29,929
-Uh-oh.

1326
00:57:29,963 --> 00:57:33,864
He's all right,
but that was close.

1327
00:57:33,898 --> 00:57:35,797
-Santa, stop, drop, and roll.

1328
00:57:35,831 --> 00:57:38,489
-Red Adair is brought in
to extinguish the fire.

1329
00:57:38,524 --> 00:57:40,526
-Watch out for the backdraft.

1330
00:57:40,560 --> 00:57:44,357
-[Cackling]

1331
00:57:44,391 --> 00:57:48,499
-Am I alone in here?
Hello?

1332
00:57:48,534 --> 00:57:50,950
-But suddenly he thinks
of something else to do.

1333
00:57:50,984 --> 00:57:54,160
-More impish pranks?
Ho, ho!

1334
00:57:54,194 --> 00:57:56,265
-Bah, he, ho, hum.

1335
00:57:59,199 --> 00:58:00,822
-That's it.

1336
00:58:00,856 --> 00:58:03,687
He'll huff and puff
until his burning breath

1337
00:58:03,721 --> 00:58:06,862
turns the doorknob
and keyhole red-hot

1338
00:58:06,897 --> 00:58:11,626
so that the magic key won't workand Santa will burn his hands.

1339
00:58:11,660 --> 00:58:14,318
-What is this,
"Home Alone 3, the Quickening"?

1340
00:58:16,700 --> 00:58:21,256
-Metal conducts heat very well,
and Satan knows that.

1341
00:58:21,290 --> 00:58:22,947
-First, he'll see
if it's hot enough.

1342
00:58:22,982 --> 00:58:24,535
-Then he'll add the clam sauce.

1343
00:58:24,570 --> 00:58:28,677
-What do you think of that?
-Not much.

1344
00:58:28,712 --> 00:58:31,266
-But Santa sees
what Pitch is up to.

1345
00:58:31,300 --> 00:58:32,543
And he isn't afraid.

1346
00:58:32,578 --> 00:58:36,789
-I'm afraid.

1347
00:58:36,823 --> 00:58:39,964
-Oh, I saw his ribs.
Ick.

1348
00:58:39,999 --> 00:58:42,622
-This place is a piece of cake.

1349
00:58:45,522 --> 00:58:47,834
-♪ Fa, la, la, la, la, la, la,
la, la, la, la ♪

1350
00:58:47,869 --> 00:58:51,217
La-la, la-la, la-la,
la-la, la-la ♪

1351
00:58:51,251 --> 00:58:55,462
-♪ Oh, the bells,
oh, the jolly, jolly bells ♪

1352
00:59:00,226 --> 00:59:02,469
-Meanwhile, Pitch looks out
the window to watch

1353
00:59:02,504 --> 00:59:03,781
Santa burn his hands

1354
00:59:03,816 --> 00:59:06,059
He doesn't seem to know
he's right behind him.

1355
00:59:06,094 --> 00:59:08,579
-Ha!

1356
00:59:08,614 --> 00:59:11,617
-It's like having Dom DeLuise
sneaking up on you.

1357
00:59:15,448 --> 00:59:16,898
-Ha, ha. Let's see.

1358
00:59:16,932 --> 00:59:19,210
A little more Tide
and the napalm's ready.

1359
00:59:19,245 --> 00:59:20,591
Heh, heh.

1360
00:59:20,626 --> 00:59:22,766
-O-ho, a cannon.

1361
00:59:22,800 --> 00:59:25,700
Now it's Santa's turn
to get even with Pitch.

1362
00:59:25,734 --> 00:59:29,566
-Now, isn't this bringing Santa
down to Satan's level?

1363
00:59:29,600 --> 00:59:31,775
Mean.

1364
00:59:31,809 --> 00:59:34,847
-Santa's a lifetime member
of the NRA.

1365
00:59:39,679 --> 00:59:41,301
-Aah! Ouch! Ow!

1366
00:59:41,336 --> 00:59:43,683
-This is funny.
I don't care what anybody says.

1367
00:59:43,718 --> 00:59:45,616
-Ow! Ow! Ouch!

1368
00:59:45,651 --> 00:59:46,721
Aah!

1369
00:59:46,755 --> 00:59:50,207
-[Laughter]
-I enjoy inflicting pain.

1370
00:59:50,241 --> 00:59:51,588
I should call the elves.

1371
00:59:51,622 --> 00:59:53,106
They'd love this.

1372
00:59:53,141 --> 00:59:55,212
-Oh, brother.

1373
00:59:55,246 --> 01:00:02,875
♪♪

1374
01:00:04,186 --> 01:00:06,637
-[Coughing]

1375
01:00:06,672 --> 01:00:09,709
-Santa burns like a tire fire.

1376
01:00:09,744 --> 01:00:13,092
-Uh, is this
the recycling center?

1377
01:00:16,026 --> 01:00:17,303
-This is the Johnson house.

1378
01:00:17,337 --> 01:00:19,063
It's the second time
I've hit them today.

1379
01:00:19,098 --> 01:00:22,446
-[Straining]

1380
01:00:22,480 --> 01:00:24,551
Just sneak in here,
and they'll never, uh,

1381
01:00:24,586 --> 01:00:26,553
have any idea
that I was ever -- Waah!

1382
01:00:28,590 --> 01:00:30,834
-Kid, you're a great audience.
Mwah.

1383
01:00:30,868 --> 01:00:34,423
[ "Jingle Bells"playing]

1384
01:00:34,458 --> 01:00:41,465
-♪ It is to ride
in Santa's underwear ♪

1385
01:00:41,499 --> 01:00:44,848
-[Sniffling] I love Christmas.

1386
01:00:44,882 --> 01:00:47,195
-Well, let's see.

1387
01:00:47,229 --> 01:00:48,679
Over-sized tomato.

1388
01:00:48,714 --> 01:00:50,957
Stock options
from the Sharper Image.

1389
01:00:50,992 --> 01:00:52,476
Lug nuts.
Cable ACE award.

1390
01:00:52,510 --> 01:00:54,443
Oh, that's no good.
Spark plug gapper.

1391
01:00:54,478 --> 01:00:56,618
Hmm.

1392
01:00:56,653 --> 01:00:58,206
-Like it?

1393
01:00:58,240 --> 01:01:03,625
♪♪

1394
01:01:03,660 --> 01:01:06,110
-Don't you wrap
any of this stuff, Santa?

1395
01:01:09,596 --> 01:01:11,944
-Oof! Ho, ho.

1396
01:01:11,978 --> 01:01:14,118
There we go.

1397
01:01:14,153 --> 01:01:16,155
Merry Chri--
Oh, shh.

1398
01:01:18,640 --> 01:01:20,607
-Hey, kid, where's the pantry?

1399
01:01:22,955 --> 01:01:25,302
-I know all those toys
don't make you happy.

1400
01:01:25,336 --> 01:01:27,822
-So I'm taking them back.
-But I'll do something for you

1401
01:01:27,856 --> 01:01:30,341
that I only do for children
who are very good.

1402
01:01:30,376 --> 01:01:33,793
-I'll sing "Proud Mary."
-I'll let you see me as I am.

1403
01:01:33,828 --> 01:01:36,451
And therefore, I will use
the powders

1404
01:01:36,485 --> 01:01:38,902
that will make you dream
that you're awake.

1405
01:01:38,936 --> 01:01:40,731
-Now, this gets weird,
so I'll warn you.

1406
01:01:40,766 --> 01:01:43,700
You may want to leave the room.

1407
01:01:43,734 --> 01:01:46,012
-And you're not allergic
to anything, are you?

1408
01:01:48,946 --> 01:01:50,741
-And now --
-A word from our sponsor.

1409
01:01:50,776 --> 01:01:53,537
-...awaken while
you're dreaming.

1410
01:01:53,571 --> 01:01:56,057
-Summer of my German
stormtrooper.

1411
01:01:58,300 --> 01:02:00,440
-He's a young Barton Fink.

1412
01:02:00,475 --> 01:02:06,308
-Uh. Uh. Hermann Goering?
Uh, oh, no, Santa.

1413
01:02:06,343 --> 01:02:07,827
-Out, vile jelly.

1414
01:02:07,862 --> 01:02:11,141
[Jazz trumpet sounds]

1415
01:02:11,175 --> 01:02:16,146
-Like what you see, kid?
-I want to be a dentist.

1416
01:02:21,013 --> 01:02:23,878
-Hey, hey, I just shined those.
-You love me, don't you?

1417
01:02:23,912 --> 01:02:26,294
Say you you love me, Santa.

1418
01:02:26,328 --> 01:02:31,437
-♪ La, la, la, la,
la, la, la, la ♪

1419
01:02:31,471 --> 01:02:35,648
-Of course I love you, sonny,
just as much as your parents.

1420
01:02:35,682 --> 01:02:36,994
-Well?

1421
01:02:37,029 --> 01:02:40,273
-Because no one loves a child
as much as his parents.

1422
01:02:40,308 --> 01:02:44,795
Only, at times, the parentsdon't understand their children,

1423
01:02:44,830 --> 01:02:48,212
and the children
don't understand their parents.

1424
01:02:48,247 --> 01:02:49,800
-Huh.
-And are you really sure

1425
01:02:49,835 --> 01:02:53,183
that they love me
when I'm left all alone?

1426
01:02:53,217 --> 01:02:55,806
-Yes, of course
they love you.

1427
01:02:55,841 --> 01:02:58,567
And you must believe
they love you.

1428
01:02:58,602 --> 01:03:00,638
And now --
-A word from our sponsors.

1429
01:03:00,673 --> 01:03:02,364
-...go back to sleep again.

1430
01:03:04,435 --> 01:03:08,198
-Phew.
I think he bought it.

1431
01:03:08,232 --> 01:03:10,096
Hey, quit drooling on my beard.

1432
01:03:10,131 --> 01:03:12,409
-It was all a sweet dream.

1433
01:03:14,894 --> 01:03:17,897
-Now, you just practice
your piano if you need love.

1434
01:03:20,037 --> 01:03:22,764
-When you awaken --
-You'll be Rick Wakeman.

1435
01:03:22,799 --> 01:03:24,904
-I wish you much happiness.

1436
01:03:24,939 --> 01:03:27,562
-And, oh, say, can I use
the can before I go?

1437
01:03:27,596 --> 01:03:30,254
-[Beeping]

1438
01:03:30,289 --> 01:03:36,502
♪♪

1439
01:03:36,536 --> 01:03:38,159
-All right, hold it, Kringle.

1440
01:03:38,193 --> 01:03:39,885
We've got the place surrounded.

1441
01:03:39,919 --> 01:03:41,162
Come out with your bag up.

1442
01:03:41,196 --> 01:03:44,717
Your reindeer have turned
themselves in.

1443
01:03:44,751 --> 01:03:47,651
-[Imitating floorboards
squeaking]

1444
01:03:50,792 --> 01:03:53,381
-Oops. No. There.
No. Oh, there we go.

1445
01:03:53,415 --> 01:03:55,417
All right, there.
Ahem.

1446
01:03:58,524 --> 01:04:01,078
-♪ That cuckoo Tannenbaum

1447
01:04:01,113 --> 01:04:02,873
-A pleasure to say hello to you.-Hi.

1448
01:04:02,908 --> 01:04:04,910
Did you leave that brat at home?-Oh, you bet.

1449
01:04:04,944 --> 01:04:06,877
He's such a pain.
-I know.

1450
01:04:06,912 --> 01:04:08,810
-Merry Christmas.
-Thank you.

1451
01:04:08,845 --> 01:04:09,880
-Goodbye, dear.
-Bye.

1452
01:04:09,915 --> 01:04:11,571
-Goodbye.
-Putz.

1453
01:04:11,606 --> 01:04:13,263
Never liked that guy.

1454
01:04:13,297 --> 01:04:15,437
-It's been a long time
since I've seen the Martins.

1455
01:04:15,472 --> 01:04:16,956
-Flaming Moe's!

1456
01:04:16,991 --> 01:04:18,958
-They're both looking pretty
well, though, aren't they?

1457
01:04:18,993 --> 01:04:22,099
-Uh, the steaming red fellow
at the bar sent these over.

1458
01:04:22,134 --> 01:04:23,756
-Oh.

1459
01:04:23,790 --> 01:04:25,896
-That's a strange cocktail,
isn't it?

1460
01:04:25,931 --> 01:04:27,553
-It's the Cocktail
of Remembrance

1461
01:04:27,587 --> 01:04:29,486
which only I can prepare.

1462
01:04:29,520 --> 01:04:32,765
Whoever drinks it will think
of that which is most dear,

1463
01:04:32,799 --> 01:04:34,905
and which, at times,
for some unknown reason

1464
01:04:34,940 --> 01:04:36,631
we seem to forget.

1465
01:04:36,665 --> 01:04:38,805
-Did I say, "I'm Pat,
and I'll be your waiter" yet?

1466
01:04:38,840 --> 01:04:41,463
-Perhaps we need a reminder.

1467
01:04:41,498 --> 01:04:44,535
Very possibly we've forgotten
someone we love.

1468
01:04:44,570 --> 01:04:45,605
-Barney.

1469
01:04:45,640 --> 01:04:47,435
-Love can be expressed
in many ways.

1470
01:04:47,469 --> 01:04:49,851
But the truest love is that
which we give

1471
01:04:49,886 --> 01:04:52,612
without expecting
anything in return.

1472
01:04:52,647 --> 01:04:54,545
-Waiter. Wai--
Waiter!

1473
01:04:54,580 --> 01:04:56,513
-Hey, can I get
some service over here?

1474
01:04:56,547 --> 01:04:58,308
Check, please.
-We really need to order.

1475
01:04:58,342 --> 01:04:59,343
We gotta hit a movie.

1476
01:04:59,378 --> 01:05:01,035
-You will become aware
of that love

1477
01:05:01,069 --> 01:05:03,002
which is closest to your heart.

1478
01:05:03,037 --> 01:05:04,935
-Oh, and keep the glass.
-They couldn't

1479
01:05:04,970 --> 01:05:07,800
drink this cocktail,
as it would burn their throats.

1480
01:05:07,834 --> 01:05:09,802
-Uh, let's just get
a bottle of wine.

1481
01:05:09,836 --> 01:05:12,701
-Well, since we are
very much in love...

1482
