01:15:28,075 --> 01:15:31,009
and a significant setback
for his campaign.

1726
01:15:31,043 --> 01:15:34,633
-[Barking]
-[Laughs]

1727
01:15:34,668 --> 01:15:36,704
-Get out.
Go away.

1728
01:15:36,739 --> 01:15:41,813
Scotch. Shoo.
Get out. Ugh.

1729
01:15:41,847 --> 01:15:43,021
-[Whimpering]

1730
01:15:43,055 --> 01:15:45,610
-That certainly was
a very funny sight,

1731
01:15:45,644 --> 01:15:47,197
old white beard
and his sack running

1732
01:15:47,232 --> 01:15:49,717
as if the Devil himself
were going to take him below.

1733
01:15:49,752 --> 01:15:53,479
-You'll pay for your mischief.
-I've got friends, Satan.

1734
01:15:53,514 --> 01:15:56,828
-Hmm. But first you'll have
to come down from that tree.

1735
01:15:56,862 --> 01:15:59,589
And I can have a lot of funbefore you can get rid of Dante.

1736
01:15:59,624 --> 01:16:01,384
Because you know
what I'm going to do?

1737
01:16:01,418 --> 01:16:03,766
I'm going to wake up everybody.

1738
01:16:03,800 --> 01:16:06,216
-Faugh!
Nobody can hear your voice.

1739
01:16:06,251 --> 01:16:07,390
-They hear it in the form

1740
01:16:07,424 --> 01:16:09,461
of their own
private imagination or ideas.

1741
01:16:09,495 --> 01:16:10,600
-Oh, now you're
just making it up.

1742
01:16:10,635 --> 01:16:12,671
-Let them see
how foolish you appear.

1743
01:16:12,706 --> 01:16:15,950
[Laughs]

1744
01:16:15,985 --> 01:16:19,575
-Toodles.
-It's Rob and Laura.

1745
01:16:22,923 --> 01:16:25,581
-There's a prowler out there.
-I want a glass of water.

1746
01:16:25,615 --> 01:16:29,205
-He's come to kill your wife
and your children.

1747
01:16:29,239 --> 01:16:32,277
He's really quite vicious.
-Give me some covers.

1748
01:16:32,311 --> 01:16:34,866
-He's hiding up in your tree.

1749
01:16:34,900 --> 01:16:36,350
Defend yourself.

1750
01:16:36,384 --> 01:16:38,524
He's going to murder you.

1751
01:16:38,559 --> 01:16:39,802
He's going to murder you.

1752
01:16:39,836 --> 01:16:43,012
-I can't stress that enough.
-[Whispering]

1753
01:16:43,046 --> 01:16:45,359
-Is it something you can share
with the whole class,

1754
01:16:45,393 --> 01:16:47,154
Mr. Lucifer?

1755
01:16:47,188 --> 01:16:49,018
-Mr. Merlin!

1756
01:16:49,052 --> 01:16:54,264
-Aw.
-Oh, no.

1757
01:16:54,299 --> 01:16:56,404
-Ooh.
-[Shouting]

1758
01:16:56,439 --> 01:16:58,475
-[Tarzan yodel]

1759
01:16:58,510 --> 01:17:01,478
-Apparently, no one is in
Santa's magic observatory.

1760
01:17:01,513 --> 01:17:02,790
-They're over at
the Keebler's place.

1761
01:17:02,825 --> 01:17:04,171
-Time to awaken.

1762
01:17:04,205 --> 01:17:05,448
There's a man outside.

1763
01:17:05,482 --> 01:17:07,726
-His name is Tim.
He asked if I could marry him.

1764
01:17:07,761 --> 01:17:10,004
Hee, hee!

1765
01:17:10,039 --> 01:17:12,731
-Marie?

1766
01:17:12,766 --> 01:17:14,733
Marie, get up.
I think that we're in danger.

1767
01:17:14,768 --> 01:17:15,976
-What?
-Yes.

1768
01:17:16,010 --> 01:17:18,634
-Oh, Rob.
-Assassin?

1769
01:17:18,668 --> 01:17:20,394
I'm not going.
-Hurry, get out of bed.

1770
01:17:20,428 --> 01:17:23,121
Go after him.
-Sure, but where's the pistol?

1771
01:17:23,155 --> 01:17:24,570
-Where you keep it.
-In the drawer?

1772
01:17:24,605 --> 01:17:25,848
-In the drawer.
-Where in the drawer?

1773
01:17:25,882 --> 01:17:28,333
In this drawer?
-The National Rifle Association

1774
01:17:28,367 --> 01:17:30,576
presents this playlet
for your enjoyment.

1775
01:17:30,611 --> 01:17:31,750
-There it is.

1776
01:17:31,785 --> 01:17:32,993
Go after him.
-Come on, don't be funny.

1777
01:17:33,027 --> 01:17:34,719
-Me?
-Yes.

1778
01:17:34,753 --> 01:17:36,997
-But I -- But I --
-El Don Knottso.

1779
01:17:37,031 --> 01:17:38,654
[Coughing]
-With this cough,

1780
01:17:38,688 --> 01:17:40,794
I can't be expected to go out.

1781
01:17:40,828 --> 01:17:42,519
I might catch pneumonia.
[Coughing]

1782
01:17:42,554 --> 01:17:44,970
-Ha.
-Ah!

1783
01:17:45,005 --> 01:17:46,696
-Come on.
Now get up.

1784
01:17:46,731 --> 01:17:48,629
Pneumonia or no pneumonia,
you go.

1785
01:17:48,664 --> 01:17:49,699
-But Marie, understand.

1786
01:17:49,734 --> 01:17:50,493
Why don't you go
and get your father?

1787
01:17:50,527 --> 01:17:51,597
-Get my father?
-Please.

1788
01:17:51,632 --> 01:17:52,840
-Wait a minute.
I must put on my robe.

1789
01:17:52,875 --> 01:17:54,359
-At home with Carl Rowan.

1790
01:17:54,393 --> 01:17:57,500
-Don't waste time.
-Rose Marie!

1791
01:17:57,534 --> 01:17:59,605
-Hi. Can I use your phone
to call my machine?

1792
01:17:59,640 --> 01:18:01,918
Thank you.

1793
01:18:01,953 --> 01:18:04,265
-I'm, uh, ordering
a Hawaiian pizza,

1794
01:18:04,300 --> 01:18:05,750
because I'm Satan.
Heh, heh.

1795
01:18:05,784 --> 01:18:07,890
-Help, police.
Help, police.

1796
01:18:07,924 --> 01:18:09,167
In the tree there's an assassin.

1797
01:18:09,201 --> 01:18:11,376
-This guy's really
an effective facilitator.

1798
01:18:11,410 --> 01:18:16,761
I'd like him on my staff.
-Grandfather!

1799
01:18:16,795 --> 01:18:19,004
-In with the bad air,
out with the good.

1800
01:18:19,039 --> 01:18:21,524
-♪ Does the Devil lose
its flavor ♪

1801
01:18:21,558 --> 01:18:23,353
♪ On the bedpost overnight?

1802
01:18:23,388 --> 01:18:26,322
[Humming]

1803
01:18:26,356 --> 01:18:28,634
-Oh, he's made out of pumice.
-Ooh.

1804
01:18:31,051 --> 01:18:35,158
-There, done and done.
[Chuckles]

1805
01:18:35,193 --> 01:18:38,058
-Hello?
I'm looking for Amanda Hugg.

1806
01:18:41,026 --> 01:18:42,648
-Fire Department.

1807
01:18:42,683 --> 01:18:43,960
Firemen.

1808
01:18:43,995 --> 01:18:45,341
Firemen!

1809
01:18:45,375 --> 01:18:47,446
The house is burning.

1810
01:18:47,481 --> 01:18:48,793
I'm on fire.

1811
01:18:48,827 --> 01:18:51,140
-The turtle called Gamera
is about to attack the city.

1812
01:18:51,174 --> 01:18:52,866
-♪ Devil with the dance belt

1813
01:18:52,900 --> 01:18:57,491
♪ Dance belt, dance belt,
devil with the dance belt on ♪

1814
01:18:57,525 --> 01:18:59,182
-It's Juan, the Maytag
repairman-o.

1815
01:18:59,217 --> 01:19:01,150
-This is a five-alarm fire.

1816
01:19:01,184 --> 01:19:04,222
Better let me have that address,please, won't you?

1817
01:19:04,256 --> 01:19:07,121
-Don't expect anything
from Santa Claus.

1818
01:19:07,156 --> 01:19:09,296
He doesn't bring toys
to poor children.

1819
01:19:09,330 --> 01:19:10,435
-What a jerk.

1820
01:19:10,469 --> 01:19:11,954
-Didn't I tell you
to keep that doll?

1821
01:19:11,988 --> 01:19:13,403
Silly.

1822
01:19:13,438 --> 01:19:16,337
So now you won't have anything.

1823
01:19:16,372 --> 01:19:19,789
You are poor.
-Mama, Mama.

1824
01:19:19,824 --> 01:19:21,515
-We must rise up
against the bourgeoisie.

1825
01:19:21,549 --> 01:19:26,106
-Don't the poor people get
anything from Santa Claus?

1826
01:19:26,140 --> 01:19:30,248
-No. Now let it rest.
-No, my darling.

1827
01:19:30,282 --> 01:19:33,044
Santa Claus is good to all of
the children who are obedient.

1828
01:19:33,078 --> 01:19:35,771
-But Santa oppresses
the proletariat.

1829
01:19:35,805 --> 01:19:37,807
-It does not matter
if they're poor or wealthy.

1830
01:19:37,842 --> 01:19:39,533
To bed now, my darling.

1831
01:19:39,567 --> 01:19:45,884
♪♪

1832
01:19:47,230 --> 01:19:49,474
-Your reindeer
will turn into powder.

1833
01:19:49,508 --> 01:19:51,441
You will starve to death.

1834
01:19:51,476 --> 01:19:54,790
And I will rule the Earth.
[Laughs]

1835
01:19:54,824 --> 01:19:57,102
[Laughter]

1836
01:19:57,137 --> 01:19:58,379
-I don't get it.

1837
01:19:58,414 --> 01:20:00,071
[Sirens]

1838
01:20:00,105 --> 01:20:04,730
-[Singing in French]

1839
01:20:04,765 --> 01:20:06,836
-I'm in control now,
right after wee-wees.

1840
01:20:06,871 --> 01:20:10,288
[Humming "William Tell
Overture"]

1841
01:20:10,322 --> 01:20:12,048
-Ever since Walter Brennan
went camp,

1842
01:20:12,083 --> 01:20:15,327
it's been all downhill.

1843
01:20:15,362 --> 01:20:16,846
-Know how this run this thing,
old man?

1844
01:20:16,881 --> 01:20:18,054
Come on, get out of my way.

1845
01:20:18,089 --> 01:20:20,643
-Santa Claus?

1846
01:20:20,677 --> 01:20:23,577
Santa Claus?

1847
01:20:23,611 --> 01:20:26,476
It's me, Merlin.

1848
01:20:26,511 --> 01:20:28,478
-Merlin.

1849
01:20:28,513 --> 01:20:30,549
-Send me a pick me up bouquet.

1850
01:20:30,584 --> 01:20:32,379
-Merlin.

1851
01:20:32,413 --> 01:20:35,934
Where are you?

1852
01:20:35,969 --> 01:20:39,248
-Here, in the observatory.
-Get out of there!

1853
01:20:39,282 --> 01:20:40,905
-What -- What is the matter?

1854
01:20:40,939 --> 01:20:43,839
In Just a few minutes,
it's going to be day.

1855
01:20:43,873 --> 01:20:45,599
Return now.

1856
01:20:45,633 --> 01:20:48,878
-They've got me in a tree,
Merlin.

1857
01:20:48,913 --> 01:20:50,811
I dropped the
Flower to Disappear.

1858
01:20:50,846 --> 01:20:51,881
-Oh, good one, Santa.

1859
01:20:51,916 --> 01:20:54,435
-And also the powders
for dreaming.

1860
01:20:54,470 --> 01:20:56,541
And this beast just
won't let me come down.

1861
01:20:56,575 --> 01:20:58,025
-Any feedback on that?

1862
01:20:58,060 --> 01:20:59,337
-All this confusion has been

1863
01:20:59,371 --> 01:21:01,270
prepared by Mr. Pitch.

1864
01:21:01,304 --> 01:21:03,272
-Wait now.

1865
01:21:03,306 --> 01:21:05,377
-Hurry, Mr. Merlin.
Hurry.

1866
01:21:05,412 --> 01:21:09,761
-Why doesn't Santa give him
another leg?

1867
01:21:09,795 --> 01:21:12,591
-[Muttering]

1868
01:21:12,626 --> 01:21:15,525
-Doh, I forgot a quarter.

1869
01:21:15,560 --> 01:21:17,665
I'll just play some pinball
while I'm waiting here.

1870
01:21:17,700 --> 01:21:19,391
Ping, ping, ping.

1871
01:21:19,426 --> 01:21:21,462
-Where can we find Santa Claus?
-I don't know.

1872
01:21:21,497 --> 01:21:23,154
That's why I got you,
Mr. Wizard.

1873
01:21:23,188 --> 01:21:26,743
-He's already been to Asia,
Europe, and Australia.

1874
01:21:26,778 --> 01:21:29,160
He must be on
the American continent.

1875
01:21:29,194 --> 01:21:30,747
-He's Rollerblading
on Venice Beach.

1876
01:21:30,782 --> 01:21:34,165
-I think I see him.
He's in Mexico.

1877
01:21:34,199 --> 01:21:35,269
Oh, golly.

1878
01:21:35,304 --> 01:21:37,858
But he's in a terrible fix.

1879
01:21:37,893 --> 01:21:40,067
And there's no time
to go to his rescue.

1880
01:21:40,102 --> 01:21:44,382
-I'm old, you see.
-And the sun is about to rise.

1881
01:21:44,416 --> 01:21:45,901
Bad dog.

1882
01:21:45,935 --> 01:21:47,972
Mad dog.
-Too much Mad Dog.

1883
01:21:48,006 --> 01:21:50,871
That's what did it.
-Against good is bad.

1884
01:21:50,906 --> 01:21:53,460
Against black is white.

1885
01:21:53,494 --> 01:21:56,359
Against a bad itch, scratch it.

1886
01:21:56,394 --> 01:21:58,637
Against thirst, water.

1887
01:21:58,672 --> 01:22:00,743
Against mad dog --
-Snap it up, Leon Russell.

1888
01:22:00,777 --> 01:22:03,711
-Against mad dog --
Against mad dog --

1889
01:22:03,746 --> 01:22:05,127
-Never mind, it's too late.
The dog got him.

1890
01:22:05,161 --> 01:22:08,337
-A cat. A cat.
A cat.

1891
01:22:08,371 --> 01:22:10,097
-This guy trained
the king of England?

1892
01:22:10,132 --> 01:22:13,031
-A cat, Santa Claus, a cat.

1893
01:22:13,066 --> 01:22:15,378
-Please be quick, Merlin.

1894
01:22:15,413 --> 01:22:17,104
Now hear this.

1895
01:22:17,139 --> 01:22:19,279
My time is almost over.

1896
01:22:19,313 --> 01:22:21,695
This time it's serious.

1897
01:22:21,729 --> 01:22:24,560
-Against mad dog, a cat.

1898
01:22:24,594 --> 01:22:28,288
Use one of the toy cats
that you wind up.

1899
01:22:28,322 --> 01:22:30,704
-Santa's tenacious jolliness
is tested

1900
01:22:30,738 --> 01:22:32,948
when he's treed by a coon hound.

1901
01:22:32,982 --> 01:22:36,192
-I didn't know Santa
and Merlin were buddies.

1902
01:22:36,227 --> 01:22:39,989
-It's a mad, mad, mad, mad, mad,mad, mad, mad,

1903
01:22:40,024 --> 01:22:42,819
mad, mad, mad, mad, mad, mad,
mad, mad, mad, mad world.

1904
01:22:44,856 --> 01:22:48,032
-So he's gonna try
and breed the dog?

1905
01:22:48,066 --> 01:22:49,516
-Don't make me laugh, Santa.

1906
01:22:49,550 --> 01:22:53,313
-Shoo. [Laughs]

1907
01:22:53,347 --> 01:22:55,280
-Ha, ha, it's a Hot Wheels cat.

1908
01:22:55,315 --> 01:22:58,490
Let's submit this
to "Doggone Funny."

1909
01:22:58,525 --> 01:23:01,977
-That's a tough driveway
to negotiate there.

1910
01:23:02,011 --> 01:23:03,564
-Let's go now.
All together now.

1911
01:23:03,599 --> 01:23:04,980
Don't push me.
Don't push me.

1912
01:23:05,014 --> 01:23:06,153
Just a minute.
You make me nervous.

1913
01:23:06,188 --> 01:23:07,913
-Oh, come on, hurry up.
-I can handle this.

1914
01:23:07,948 --> 01:23:09,570
But don't leave me alone, huh?
-All right.

1915
01:23:09,605 --> 01:23:12,263
We're with you.
Come on.

1916
01:23:12,297 --> 01:23:14,403
-♪ Indiana wants me

1917
01:23:14,437 --> 01:23:17,682
♪ Lord, I can't go back there

1918
01:23:17,716 --> 01:23:20,098
-Where's the body?
How many are injured?

1919
01:23:20,133 --> 01:23:22,031
-[Gasp] Hosni Mubarak.

1920
01:23:22,066 --> 01:23:25,241
-They'll surely find Santa.

1921
01:23:25,276 --> 01:23:27,347
-Nothing in sight.
-We surely can't find Santa.

1922
01:23:27,381 --> 01:23:30,384
-Can't see anything.
Better look around.

1923
01:23:30,419 --> 01:23:32,110
-Don't push me.
Leave me alone.

1924
01:23:32,145 --> 01:23:33,387
Don't do that.

1925
01:23:33,422 --> 01:23:35,286
Hello. Hello.

1926
01:23:35,320 --> 01:23:36,390
Well, why don't you shoot?

1927
01:23:36,425 --> 01:23:38,427
-It's the last episode
of "AKA Pablo."

1928
01:23:38,461 --> 01:23:39,635
-Be careful.
It may be a whole gang.

1929
01:23:39,669 --> 01:23:40,808
But don't worry.
Try to be brave.

1930
01:23:40,843 --> 01:23:42,327
Be calm.
We must all be brave.

1931
01:23:42,362 --> 01:23:43,466
That's it, the hole.

1932
01:23:43,501 --> 01:23:45,330
-[Shrieking]

1933
01:23:45,365 --> 01:23:49,576
-Montgomery, Alabama, 1955.
-We're wet!

1934
01:23:49,610 --> 01:23:51,888
-Hurry.
You barely have time now.

1935
01:23:51,923 --> 01:23:53,959
-I still have one more friend
to visit.

1936
01:23:53,994 --> 01:23:55,651
I mustn't fail her.
-But --

1937
01:23:55,685 --> 01:23:57,239
-No "buts" about it.

1938
01:23:57,273 --> 01:23:59,034
First come the children.

1939
01:23:59,068 --> 01:24:02,244
I'll see you later, if possible.

1940
01:24:02,278 --> 01:24:03,521
-Well, he was here, all right.

1941
01:24:03,555 --> 01:24:04,867
This is definitely Santa scat.

1942
01:24:04,901 --> 01:24:06,420
-What happened?
Did you find anyone?

1943
01:24:06,455 --> 01:24:07,973
-We've looked
all over the place.

1944
01:24:08,008 --> 01:24:10,355
-Wow, I'm insane, huh?

1945
01:24:10,390 --> 01:24:13,358
-Let's make sure the fire's out.

1946
01:24:13,393 --> 01:24:15,981
-It's out.
-There's some smoke over there.

1947
01:24:18,881 --> 01:24:21,780
-Well, that serves him right,
the old troublemaker.

1948
01:24:21,815 --> 01:24:23,920
He'll probably catch pneumonia.

1949
01:24:23,955 --> 01:24:26,026
But he asked for it.
-Isn't he immortal?

1950
01:24:26,061 --> 01:24:28,580
What does he care
about pneumonia?

1951
01:24:28,615 --> 01:24:31,100
-Wait.
The Flower to Disappear

1952
01:24:31,135 --> 01:24:34,207
has fallen
right into Lupita's house.

1953
01:24:34,241 --> 01:24:37,555
-Just take my word on this.
It really happened.

1954
01:24:37,589 --> 01:24:40,075
-Yeah, I wanted to be
a figure skater.

1955
01:24:40,109 --> 01:24:41,835
I could have beat Peggy Fleming.

1956
01:24:41,869 --> 01:24:43,630
Could have been
on the "Sullivan Show."

1957
01:24:43,664 --> 01:24:45,701
Yeah, I could have had
Senor Wences' hand.

1958
01:24:45,735 --> 01:24:47,806
Uh, in marriage, I mean.

1959
01:24:47,841 --> 01:24:50,568
Yeah, I could
have been somebody.

1960
01:24:50,602 --> 01:24:51,810
Oh, no.

1961
01:24:51,845 --> 01:24:54,330
[Mumbling]

1962
01:24:54,365 --> 01:24:58,576
-Diarrhea is like a storm
raging outside your home.

1963
01:24:58,610 --> 01:25:03,201
-I think the Wallendas
are sneaking in.

1964
01:25:03,236 --> 01:25:04,927
-Well, bring me up, Walt.

1965
01:25:04,961 --> 01:25:08,033
[Snapping sound]

1966
01:25:08,068 --> 01:25:09,069
-Oops.
-Raus!

1967
01:25:09,104 --> 01:25:11,036
[Screaming in German]

1968
01:25:11,071 --> 01:25:17,250
♪♪

